"""Generated from Smithy shape ``com.amazonaws.partnercentralmarketing#TaggableResourceArn``."""

from typing import TypeAlias

"""The ARN of a taggable Partner Central Marketing resource. One resource type is taggable — the campaign: arn:aws:partnercentral:{region}:{account}:catalog/{Catalog}/campaign/{CampaignId} Nothing else is taggable, and the pattern admits nothing else. A campaign asset has no ARN at all: every asset operation authorizes on its campaign, and `aws:ResourceTag` on one resolves the campaign's tags, so an asset tag could never affect access (DG-063 D-20). A social connection has an ARN but is not taggable. Reference materials no longer exist. `{account}` is the partner's own account — the caller's — not the service account, mirroring `PartnerArnHelper.buildPartnerArn` in AWSPartnerEntityService. Both region and account are always populated: Tagris's `ArnStateMachineProcessor.getRegionRequirement` treats a vendor with no explicit region map as REQUIRED, so an ARN omitting either fails to parse. Templates are deliberately absent. They are AWS-authored and platform-managed — read-only API surface, no customer account in their partition key, seeded by an internal script — so they fall under the "AWS Service owned resources" exemption rather than being customer-taggable. The ARN service field is the shared Partner Central family code `partnercentral`, not this service's `partnercentral-marketing` facet (which names the endpoint, SigV4 signing name and CloudTrail event source). The pattern follows the sibling Partner Central services (PartnerCentralBenefitsServiceModel, PartnerIntegrationAPIModel), which share that service field. `Campaign` is a literal and the id segment excludes `/`, so no other resource type and no nested form matches. The service's own type check stays as a second line, for a stage that runs without model validation."""
TaggableResourceArn: TypeAlias = str
